# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# Keywords uppercase themselves as they are typed, 1982-style: when a
# non-word character or a Return ENDS a word the interpreter reserves,
# the editor shouts it -- but only where the word is CODE, so a keyword
# inside a string stays as it was typed.  And the shout is ONE journal
# batch: a single undo puts the word back as the hands left it.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note a keyword typed lower-case, then a space -- and it is uppercased
key p
key r
key i
key n
key t
wait 3
key space
wait 6
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 10 PRINT
note a keyword INSIDE a string is left exactly as typed: PRINT here is
note code and shouts, goto is inside the quotes and does not
key Return
wait 8
key p
key r
key i
key n
key t
key space
wait 4
key "
key g
key o
key t
key o
wait 3
key space
wait 6
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 20 PRINT "goto
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas GOTO
note the shout is ONE undo away from what was typed: two undos -- the
note space, then the whole re-cased word as a batch -- give back "let"
key Return
wait 8
key l
key e
key t
wait 3
key space
wait 6
key z ctrl
wait 4
key z ctrl
wait 6
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 let
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 LET
quit
